    <section class="section">
      <div class="container two-col">
        <div class="prose">
          <h2>Not an emergency — a booking</h2>
          <p>This is different from the rest of our services. Where <a href="breakdown-recovery-birmingham.html">breakdown recovery</a> and <a href="accident-recovery-birmingham.html">accident recovery</a> respond to something that's gone wrong on the road, car transport is arranged in advance for a car that simply needs to move from one place to another. There's no roadside urgency involved — you tell us where the car is, where it needs to go, and when, and we work around your schedule, anywhere across <a href="../areas/birmingham.html">Birmingham</a> and the West Midlands.</p>

          <h2>Common reasons people book car transport</h2>
          <ul class="checklist">
            <li><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true"><polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"/></svg> A car bought at auction or from a dealer that needs collecting and bringing home.</li>
            <li><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true"><polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"/></svg> A private sale purchase that isn't roadworthy yet.</li>
            <li><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true"><polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"/></svg> A non-runner being moved into storage.</li>
            <li><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true"><polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"/></svg> Moving a car between home addresses.</li>
            <li><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true"><polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"/></svg> A planned move to or from a garage, for work booked in advance.</li>
            <li><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true"><polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"/></svg> A car that has failed its MOT and can no longer be legally driven.</li>
          </ul>

          <h2>How booking works</h2>
          <p>Get in touch with the collection address, the destination, and roughly when you'd like the move to happen. Let us know whether the car is driveable, since that affects how it's loaded, and whether there's anything unusual about access at either end, such as a narrow driveway or a locked compound. We'll confirm the details and arrange a suitable time.</p>

          <div class="callout">
            <p><strong>Driving without an MOT.</strong> A car that has failed its MOT, or has none, generally can't be driven on the public road except to a small number of permitted destinations such as a pre-booked test. Transporting it on a recovery vehicle avoids that problem entirely, since the car isn't being driven at all.</p>
          </div>

          <h2>When you might need something else instead</h2>
          <p>If your car has actually broken down and you need it collected right now, our <a href="breakdown-recovery-birmingham.html">breakdown recovery</a> or general <a href="car-recovery-birmingham.html">car recovery</a> pages cover that kind of urgent situation. Car transport is the better fit whenever there's no emergency and you're simply planning a move.</p>
        </div>

